body:
- **CI/CD:** GitHub Actions on pull_request and push to `main`, `v0.*` and `build/**`, per-ref concurrency with cancel-in-progress (.github/workflows/ci.yml:); jobs MSRV build (Rust 1.91), default build, default test, counter build, wasm examples build, rustfmt, clippy, CI-script tests, docs, dependency audit, accessibility (a11y) tests, coverage report, stand checks repeated (`stand-repeat`, since 2026-10-14-quality-gates: `ubuntu-latest`, needing the fast four, the test job's `workspace-test` cache restored with `save-if: false`, a failure-only `ci-log-stand-repeat` upload, no job-level permission; .github/workflows/ci.yml:), cross-platform matrix (.github/workflows/ci.yml:), under a workflow-level `permissions: contents: read` with no job-level grant (.github/workflows/ci.yml:), split fast/slow — `fmt`, `clippy`, `test-features-default` and `ci-scripts` carry no `needs`, and every other job (the matrix included) `needs` all four (.github/workflows/ci.yml:; .github/workflows/ci.yml:); each of the thirteen linux jobs (twelve until 2026-10-14-quality-gates) runs its leg as `bash .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh {leg}`, the same command the dev host runs, with `--locked` on every cargo leg but `fmt`, `cargo fmt --all --check` (.github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:), and `examples/wasm_hello` (.github/workflows/ci.yml:; .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:); the docs job runs `cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --locked` (.github/workflows/ci.yml:; .github/scripts/ci-leg.sh:), an effective rustdoc `-D warnings` gate over every workspace library crate — green on the dev host and in CI run 37386253475, as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-05-ci-gate-legs/evidence/gates.md; nine Ubuntu jobs — build-msrv, build-features-default, test-features-default, build-counter, clippy, doc, a11y, coverage and, since 2026-10-14-quality-gates, stand-repeat
 — install `libfontconfig1-dev` through `bash .github/scripts/apt-install.sh libfontconfig1-dev` and build the profiles unrewritten — no `opt-level` rewrite step (.github/workflows/ci.yml:); every package install of ci.yml is bounded and retried — no line of it calls `apt-get`, ten `run:` steps call that script (§Standard Contracts → CI contracts; nine until 2026-10-14-quality-gates), the tenth the `ci-scripts` job's guarded `python3-yaml` step, and the matrix job's `Install apt deps` step, a third-party action, carries `timeout-minutes: 10`, the file's one step timeout, with no job-level timeout (.github/workflows/ci.yml:; .github/workflows/ci.yml:) — green in CI#37985678276, where the eight `libfontconfig1-dev` calls took 10 to 16 s each and the guarded call was not reached, as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-09-audit-corrections-agent-surfaces/evidence/operator-pass.md; matrix tests windows and macos (`--all --tests`) and only builds ios and android, android via `cross`, each `--locked` under `shell: bash` with its output tee'd to `target/ci-logs/matrix-{platform}.log`; linux is tested by the fast `test` leg, not the matrix (.github/workflows/ci.yml:; .github/workflows/ci.yml:); `Swatinem/rust-cache` (SHA-pinned, `# v2`) on every compiling ci.yml job but `coverage` saves on `refs/heads/main` and `refs/heads/build/*`, except `a11y` and, since 2026-10-14-quality-gates, `stand-repeat`, which restore the test job's `workspace-test` key and never save (.github/workflows/ci.yml:; .github/workflows/ci.yml:; .github/workflows/ci.yml:; .github/workflows/ci.yml:; .github/workflows/ci.yml:);
 every ci.yml `uses:` is pinned to a 40-hex commit SHA and every `dtolnay/rust-toolchain` step names its `toolchain` (.github/scripts/test_ci_workflows.py:), while publish-browser's and wpt's caches save only on `refs/heads/main` (.github/workflows/publish-browser.yml:; .github/workflows/wpt.yml:); every leg job uploads its own log on failure, kept 7 days, and the `coverage` job also uploads its `coverage-report` on success, kept 7 days (.github/workflows/ci.yml:; .github/workflows/ci.yml:); wasm_hello described as a standalone workspace, seven_guis and todomvc built as wasm cdylib with `--no-default-features --features hybrid` (.github/workflows/ci.yml:); WPT job 15-minute timeout running `cargo run -rp wpt css svg`, zstd-compressing, scoring with `wpt` cli "0.0.14", diffing against main and deploying Pages on main (.github/workflows/wpt.yml:; .github/workflows/wpt.yml:); the WPT, post-results and publish workflows run only on `DioxusLabs/blitz` (repository guard on every job — .github/workflows/wpt.yml:; .github/workflows/wpt.yml:; .github/workflows/wpt-post-results.yml:; .github/workflows/publish-browser.yml:)

- **Tests:** unit tests in `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` at the end of the source file (apps/browser/src/about_pages.rs:; apps/browser/src/browser_history.rs:; apps/browser/src/favicon.rs:; apps/browser/src/url_suggestions.rs:; apps/browser/persistence/src/lib.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/net.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo_to_parley.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/util.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/scrollbar.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/element.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/fuzzy.rs:; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/js_wrapper.rs:; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/harness_test.rs:; wpt/runner/src/test_runners/mod.rs:); eight unit-test modules sit in files of their own, each a `#[cfg(test)]` child declared through `#[path]` at its parent — dioxus-native-dom's bridge tests, declared at the end of `dioxus_document.rs` as `#[cfg(test)] #[path = "dioxus_document_tests.rs"] mod bridge_tests;`, a child of the module under test so they reach its private fields with no constructor, `pub` or `cfg(test)` shim added (packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/dioxus_document.rs:), and, since 2026-10-16-file-splits, blitz-dom's `document::changed_set_tests` and `document::font_reading_tests` in `document_changed_set_tests.rs` and `document_font_reading_tests.rs` (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:) and escher-driver's `mcp::tests` and `schema::tests` in `mcp_tests.rs` and `schema_tests.rs` (packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:; packages/escher-driver/src/schema.rs:), each moved out whole with its test paths unchanged;
 each integration test file covers one behavior and opens with a `//!` doc naming the behavior and any guarded bug (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_leak.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/comment_layout.rs:); regression tests cite upstream issue or PR URLs (tests/blitz-tests/tests/animations.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/render_blocking_stylesheet.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_interaction_state.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_node_mapping.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/custom_widget_layout.rs:); documents built with `HtmlDocument::from_html` and a `DocumentConfig` with a `ColorScheme::Light` viewport and `HtmlProvider`, then `resolve(0.0)` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/comment_layout.rs:); scenarios run in both layout modes `for incremental in [false, true]` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_cache_invalidation.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/flex_grid_order.rs:); descriptive snake_case test names (tests/blitz-tests/tests/dir_attribute.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/dir_attribute.rs:); `#[track_caller]` assertion helpers (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_roles.rs:); some tests use `test_that` matchers returning `TestResult<()>` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/accessibility_hidden.rs:); a pointer-event builder is repeated per file (tests/blitz-tests/tests/details_element.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/fragment_navigation.rs:;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/scrollbar_drag.rs:), while the seven_guis stand checks state the tables and helpers they share once, in the module `tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs`, which a check reads by declaring `mod common;` — a module in a subdirectory of the integration-test directory is no test target, so each test-target file still covers one behavior (tests/blitz-tests/tests/common/mod.rs:) — and the checks that hold a `Session` — the session checks, the settle check `stand_settle`, the sixteen driver-action checks `stand_act_*`, since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface `stand_mcp_tools`, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, `stand_screenshot_repeat` and, since 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, the driver sweep `stand_requirement_sweep`, and the served-page checks `stand_cells_served` and `stand_load_page` — keep what they share in a second such module, `tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs`, read by `mod session_common;` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/session_common/mod.rs:); tests first assert the fixture produces the condition under test (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_leak.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/interaction_state_canonicalization.rs:); WPT test names use forward slashes relative to WPT_DIR (wpt/runner/src/main.rs:); the CI Python tests use `unittest` with one `TestCase` per function (.github/scripts/test_wpt_diff_to_pr.py:; .github/scripts/test_wpt_diff_to_pr.py:); blitz-tests keeps one test target per file directly under `tests/` — its `[package]` sets no `autotests` — and the one file there that is declared and never built is upstream's single-binary `tests/all.rs`, the manifest's one `[[test]]` table, held at `test = false`: the operator's decision of 2026-10-10, a standing two-line difference from upstream's manifest that `BlitzTestsTargetsTest` pins (tests/blitz-tests/Cargo.toml:; .github/scripts/test_blitz_tests_targets.py:)

- **Invalidation and state integrity:** interaction state referencing a removed node is cleared or retargeted before the node is freed (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:); element-state changes take a state-only snapshot only when a rule depends on those bits (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:); damaged elements mark their ancestor chain (packages/blitz-dom/src/stylo.rs:); damage propagates up the DOM and to anonymous ancestors via `layout_parent` (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:); non-incremental mode marks every node `ALL_DAMAGE` (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:); damage and dirty flags cleared in one visit per node, skipping clean subtrees (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:); stale slab ids tolerated by `get`/`contains_key` (packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/damage.rs:); `dirty_descendants` and `damaged_descendants` ancestor invariants (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/stale_dirty_descendants.rs:; tests/blitz-tests/tests/style_property_invalidation.rs:); new Stylo element data marked `ALL_DAMAGE` (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/stylo_data.rs:); anonymous blocks exist only in `layout_children` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_cache_invalidation.rs:); every DOM mutation inserts `CONSTRUCT_BOX` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/anonymous_block_cache_invalidation.rs:); geometry memoisation invalidated by a generation counter (packages/blitz-dom/src/tree.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/tree.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:); animations, transitions and smooth scrolls advance via `resolve(time)` and `is_animating()` (tests/blitz-tests/tests/pseudo_element_update.rs:;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/fragment_navigation.rs:); a color-scheme change recascades everything (tests/blitz-tests/tests/device_coalescing.rs:); reading the stylist device flushes pending changes (tests/blitz-tests/tests/device_coalescing.rs:); the changed set (§Standard Contracts → Document core) is written at five kinds of site — the 15 mutation-flag sites of `DocumentMutator`, each marking the node whose in-document flag its own condition reads and only when that condition holds (the node itself in `set_node_text`, `append_text_to_node`, `set_attribute`, `clear_attribute`, `set_style_property`, `remove_style_property`, `set_sub_document`, `remove_sub_document`, `set_custom_widget`, `remove_custom_widget`, `remove_node` and `remove_and_drop_node_with`, the parent in `remove_and_drop_all_children` and `add_children_to_parent`, the moved child in `add_children_to_parent`); `snapshot_node_and` when its `ElementState` argument intersects `FOCUS` or `CHECKED`, so a focus move, a checkbox toggle and `toggle_radio` (which marks every radio of the set, changed or not); the `Input` arm of `apply_generated_text_input_event` (a typed character, an IME commit), the last two wherever the node is, in the document or not; and, since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction, `BaseDocument::apply_range_move`, which marks a range input where a key or a pointerdown changed its value and nothing for a move that changes nothing (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:), and `BaseDocument::apply_select_choice`, which marks a select where a key or typeahead or, on a `multiple` select or a single select's open list, a click on a row (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:) changed its chosen option or set and nothing for a choice of the chosen option (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:) — and, with no select list standing, is not written by node creation, hover, active, scroll, a viewport resize, a resource load, an animation or layout, so a `resolve` with nothing written marks nothing in either layout mode;
 the fifth kind of site is a select's list: its opening or closing marks the select, a page scroll or a move of the select's box that closes the list marks it through `reconcile_select_list` at the next resolve, a wheel elsewhere marks it through `close_select_list`, and a highlight or a wheel move inside the list marks nothing (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:);
 the set is engine-touched, a superset of what a snapshot reads as changed (an attribute re-written to itself marks and changes no reading; bounds-only movement changes a reading and marks nothing); ratified by the founder (2026-10-07), the engine half of the item §Document core records (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:) — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-change-tracking-and-diff/report.md; under `accessibility` the shell rebuilds the platform accessibility tree on a poll that reported work when the changed set that poll took was non-empty — not on every document change — and takes the set on every such poll with or without the feature; ratified by the founder (2026-10-07), the shell half of the same item, its windowed witness still owed (packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:); colour scheme follows the window theme with an override, default Light (packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:; packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:; packages/blitz-shell/src/window.rs:)

- **[Scrolling and input]** Root element scroll applies to the viewport per CSS overflow propagation (packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:), and the root element does not clip its own overflow (packages/blitz-paint/src/render.rs:); viewport scroll offset lives on `NodeTree` (packages/blitz-dom/src/tree.rs:); `overflow: hidden` axes are scrollable programmatically but not by the user (packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:); user scrolls chain unconsumed delta to the viewport, a `scroll_to` or a `scroll_by` clamps to one scroller and chains nothing (packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:), and `scroll_into_view` writes every scrolling box on its target's containing-block chain, innermost first, and then the viewport, a row of an open select list excepted (§Standard Contracts → Scrolling, selection, tree) — each nested write an instant `scroll_to` clamped to its own box, the requested behaviour applying to the viewport alone, so an into-view scroll never animates a nested box (packages/blitz-dom/src/scrolling.rs:; ratified by the founder, 2026-10-07: the method itself is widened for every document, no second method beside it — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-refusal-detection/report.md); a box's client rect is the box's own — the shared bounds reader subtracts the scroll offset of every box on the containing-block chain above a node and never the node's own — and, an open select list answering first above that walk, a hit stops at the padding box of every box paint clips — one that clips by `overflow`, on one axis or both, or one whose computed `contain` includes `paint` on a box paint applies it to (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18) — the root element excepted (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/writing_mode.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:;
 the founder's ruling, 2026-10-10, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed by the overseer: both fixed in the engine, each a direct change for every document, ahead of the MCP surface; how far each reaches — the fix made in the shared reader, the stop at paint's overflow half — is the operator's answer of that day, and the second reader `Node::absolute_position` subtracts only its containing blocks' scroll offsets (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18; §Standard Contracts → Scrolling, selection, tree); both are flagged upstreamable, cut against upstream `main` at 7832c177, and no upstream pull request is open — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-scrolling-box-bounds-and-hit/report.md); a third direct engine change for every document stands beside those two since 2026-10-10-snapshot-states, in the accessibility builder's own file: the builder writes AccessKit's `selected`, `toggled` and `invalid` on an element's node from `aria-selected`, `aria-pressed` and `aria-invalid`, read by value (a select's option excepted, its `selected` its chosen state, [DOM semantics]) — `toggled` from `aria-checked` in place of `aria-pressed` on a checkable role, and from neither attribute on a native checkbox or radio (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18), which writes `Toggled::True` or `False` from its own `checkbox_input_checked()` under a checkable role and nothing under any other (§Standard Contracts → Mutation, query and CSSOM)
 — ratified by the founder (2026-10-10, by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label «Ратифицировать», the English wording is the overseer's: the builder writes the three states on the node, and what an assistive technology reads of them stays unmeasured until the windowed check), flagged upstreamable against the same 7832c177, where `accessibility.rs` reads +57 −1 against that ref and read +26 −0 before the chunk (the local ref, not fetched), and no upstream pull request is open (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs: — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-snapshot-states/report.md); a fifth direct engine change for every document stands beside the three this decision counts and the password paint under [Painting] since 2026-10-13-range-input-interaction, the range interaction model: an `input` whose `type` reads `range` (ASCII case-insensitive) holds its current value apart from its `value` attribute (`RangeInputData`, §Standard Contracts → Nodes and widgets), its rules written against the WHATWG range state in `node/range.rs` — `min` 0 and `max` 100 by default, a `max` below `min` reading `min`, `step` 1 by default, a step ≤ 0 or unparsable reading 1 and `any` setting no grid, the step base `min`, else the `value` attribute, else 0, the default value the midpoint, and every value sanitized to `[min, max]` and the nearest grid value, the greater on a tie (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/range.rs:); focused and with no `disabled` attribute (presence), `ArrowRight` and `ArrowUp` step it up, `ArrowLeft` and `ArrowDown` step it down, `Home` and `End` take it to its minimum and maximum, and every other key does nothing (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:);
 a main-button pointerdown sets the value from the hit's fraction of the content box, clamped to [0, 1], a box of no width reading 0, and a click focuses it and changes no value, so a label's synthetic click focuses without moving it (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:); each change fires one `input` event and a move that changes nothing fires none (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:); a `value` write re-seeds the current value and a `min`, `max` or `step` write or removal re-sanitizes it — a departure from the spec's dirty-value flag, the cost the founder's first fork answer took on so that a Dioxus re-render keeps control (packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:); form submission sends the formatted current value (packages/blitz-dom/src/form.rs:); before it no key or click moved a range input and a click did not focus it (measured at 2026-10-07-act-by-id) — ratified by the founder: his ruling of 2026-10-07 «Пусть будет а», his answers to the three forks of 2026-10-13 «Отдельное текущее значение», «Стрелки + Home/End (Рекомендую)» and «Клик даёт фокус (Рекомендую)», and his confirm of the wrap's answer card the same day «Подтвердить (Рекомендую)», which also covers the three consequences the operator confirmed at the review (submission sends the current value, a `value` write resets it, the pointerdown moves the value and the click focuses) — each by question dialog in the overseer session, relayed verbatim by the overseer as his chosen option label, the English wording the overseer's;
 flagged upstreamable against upstream `main` at 434e0661, which has no range interaction, and no upstream pull request is open; its merge surface is `node/element.rs`, `node/mod.rs`, `layout/construct.rs`, `mutator.rs`, `events/keyboard.rs`, `events/pointer.rs` and `form.rs`, with the new `node/range.rs`, read at upstream `main` `e72650a6` on 2026-10-15, three commits past that base, and untouched by upstream since it — `git diff --stat 434e0661 e72650a6` over it empty, as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-quality-gates/evidence/merge-surface.md — as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-13-range-input-interaction/report.md; at upstream `main` `ebacd68bd` the taken commits reach `node/element.rs`, `layout/construct.rs` and `mutator.rs`, the one conflict `mutator.rs`'s `set_attribute`, resolved by placing upstream's `open` arm after the range re-sanitize arm (`min` · `max` · `step` → `resanitize_range_input`) as a second independent `if` (as measured at escher-0.3.0/chunks/2026-10-27-upstream-sync-engine-debts/evidence/take.md); three more direct engine changes for every document stand beside those since 2026-10-13-stand-keyboard-harness, the sixth to the eighth: keyboard activation — a pressed `Enter` whose target is the focused node, after the text-input and range arms, dispatches a Click on it when it is no disabled form control ([DOM semantics]) and is a `button`, a `summary`, an `input` of type `submit`, `reset` or `button`, or an `a` with `href`, and a released Space on the focused node dispatches the same Click, through the new `handle_key_up`, for a `button`, a `summary`, or an `input` of type `submit`, `reset`, `button`, `checkbox` or `radio` that is not disabled — a link takes no Space, and a text input and a range input take neither key there — the Click's data built from `Node::synthetic_click_event_data(modifiers)` and queued by the event driver, so the app's handlers run before the default action `handle_click` (packages/blitz-dom/src/events